  "id": "unconditional-positive-regard",
  "term": "unconditional positive regard",
  "definition": "Unconditional positive regard is one of the Rogerian core conditions and a basic principle of person-centered therapy. It refers to a therapist’s accepting, responsive stance toward the client within the therapeutic relationship, as part of a relational framework that emphasizes presence and attunement rather than fixed techniques.",
